course: dictionary
lesson: 3704
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives flea two meanings: a very small jumping insect, and a flea market, where people sell old things cheaply. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «A vet gives pets flea treatment» is about insects, because a treatment is something you give to get rid of a problem on a pet. «We found a cheap lamp at the flea market» is about a market, because you buy things at a market.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. A flea can jump about 30 centimetres, and that only makes sense for the insect, not the market. Clues like bite, jump and treatment point to the insect. Clues like sell, cheap and stall point to the market.
fact: Flea is a noun: one flea, or two or more fleas.
fact: «Flea» means a very small jumping insect without wings that lives on the skin and fur of animals and people and sucks their blood.
fact: «Flea market» means a market where people sell old and second-hand things cheaply.
fact: «Fleas» are tiny wingless insects with six legs, and the back pair is long and strong for jumping.
fact: «A flea in your ear» is a British phrase that means a scolding.
exercise: «A cat flea can jump about 30 centimetres, many times its body length.» What is a flea in this sentence? | A market where old things are sold | A kind of cat food | *A tiny jumping insect | A small wooden boat
exercise: «We went to the flea market on Saturday to buy an old clock.» What does flea market mean? | *A market where people sell old and second-hand things cheaply | A jumping competition | A place to sleep | A dog show
exercise: In «A vet gives pets flea treatment», which word is the best clue that flea means an insect? | The word gives | *The word treatment, because you treat a problem | The word people | The word vet
test: «Fleas are tiny wingless insects with six legs.» What does wingless mean? | *Without wings | Very fast | With very big wings | Hungry all the time
test: «The Black Death spread in the 1340s, its germs carried by traders, animals, goods and fleas.» In this sentence, flea means | A market stall | A flat boat | *A tiny insect | A type of cloth
exam: Which sentence uses flea to mean a market? | «The flea jumped 30 centimetres.» | *«We found a cheap chair at the flea market.» | «Lice and fleas are pests.» | «The vet gave a flea treatment.»
